      "id": "8",
      "type": "details",
      "attributes": {
        "key": "documentation",
        "value": "A column family is a container for columns, like the table in a relational system.\nA column family holds an ordered list of columns, which you can reference by the column name.\nFor all column families, each row is uniquely identified by its row key, similar to the primary key in a relational table. A column family is always partitioned on its row key, and the row key is always implicitly indexed.\n"
      }
